diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 7456e1c..d29a9c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,28 @@
 
 Tests: `cd backend && npm test` (needs local MongoDB) and `cd frontend && npm test`.
 To lock another page: wrap it with `<PinLock section="budgets">` in `App.jsx` and add `router.use(requirePinUnlock('budgets'))` in its routes file.
+
+
+## R19 - Automated Reminders
+
+* **Settings** (Reminders page): in-app/browser notifications, e-mail reminders, daily "log your expenses" reminder at a chosen time, bill-due reminders (N days before + on the due day). Times use the user's own time zone.
+* **Bills**: add bills (one-time or monthly) with a due date. Monthly bills roll forward automatically; "mark paid" moves them to next month.
+* **How it works**: `services/cronService.js` runs `runReminderCycle()` every minute (node-cron). A unique `(user, dedupeKey)` index guarantees a reminder is never sent twice. E-mail goes through Nodemailer (`services/emailService.js`); without `SMTP_*` in `.env` mails are only printed in the server console.
+* The bell in the navbar shows unread reminders and pops a browser notification for new ones (while the app is open).
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET / PUT | `/api/reminders/settings` | notification settings |
+| POST | `/api/reminders/test` | send a test reminder now |
+| GET / POST | `/api/reminders` | list / add bills |
+| PUT / DELETE | `/api/reminders/:id` | edit / delete a bill |
+| POST | `/api/reminders/:id/paid` | mark a bill paid |
+| GET | `/api/notifications` | bell list + unread count |
+| PUT | `/api/notifications/:id/read`, `/read-all` | mark read |
+
+## R20 - Audit Log / Activity History
+
+* Every create / update / delete of accounts and bills, profile & security changes (PIN, privacy) and logins are recorded in `AuditLog`. Only field **names** are stored, never values (no balances, passwords or PINs).
+* **Activity** page: search, filter by action / type / date range, pagination. The log is append-only (the model refuses updates and deletes, and there are no edit/delete endpoints).
+* `GET /api/audit?action=&entityType=&from=&to=&search=&page=&limit=` - users only see their own history.
+* To log a new module (e.g. transactions): `router.post('/', audit('CREATE', 'Transaction'), createTransaction)` using `audit` from `middleware/auditMiddleware.js` (add the name to `config/auditConstants.js` if it is new). For custom events call `logActivity(req, {...})`.
